    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="0899" n="883" xml:id="pg883"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711F.1914/1–1747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Panama </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-20T19:00:00-05:00">January 20, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. It appears urtel 33 Jan 17 Fonmin plan contains factors which this Govt
                    consistently has found basically objectionable. Dept most anxious for progress
                    on new defense agreement and thereafter to meet Panama’s justifiable requests on
                    other pending matters. Accordingly, Dept feels it advisable send Murray
                        Wise<anchor n="6" xml:id="d757-f1"/> to Emb with Dept’s instructions to
                    assist in pressing negotiation these matters. If this proposal agreeable to you
                    Wise would plan arrive Panama by Sun 26. Please advise immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d757-f1" n="6" xml:id="d757-f1-content">
                <p>Assistant Chief, Division of Central America and Panama Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
